;; talk/institution--canon.scm — objections to surfaces/institution.scm from the lens of canon.

(objection 'o-institution-canon-1 :by "sonnet-canon" :to 'd-institution-who :lens "canon"
  :claim (canon 'rejected-ideas-need-new-evidence "An idea on docs/rejected-ideas.md needs new evidence written into its decision before it is proposed. That list says the owner rejected selling provable payment authorization to corporate treasuries as the angle. The surface is that idea in full: several signers, a vote before money moves, and a record an outside auditor can check against the signed history. The decision answers that this is an organisation that uses xln and not the sales angle, but its own because-clause marks this as a guess, and a reading is not evidence. The cost is a whole surface, seven screens and nine flows, built on an idea the owner closed. Whether this reading is allowed is the maintainer's to say; d-institution-who names the question and nothing in the file shows an answer, and its decider is the user although the rule is the maintainer's."))

(objection 'o-institution-canon-2 :by "sonnet-canon" :to 'institution-spare-cash :lens "canon"
  :claim (canon 'lending-reopened "Lending must appear with exact amounts, who holds authority, deadlines and recovery. This screen shows principal, rate, interest so far and term. The late window, how long interest keeps running after maturity, exists in the ground (loan-late-window) and is not shown. Neither the screen nor institution-savings-flow says what the organisation can do if the hub does not pay out on time, or who can end the position. The cost is a board that votes to place spare cash and sees a term but not the point after which the money is late and what then protects it. The flow ends by saying the hub completes the payout, which states who acts and not what recovery the organisation has. The rule is already the maintainer's; no decision in the file concerns recovery for savings."))

(objection 'o-institution-canon-3 :by "sonnet-canon" :to 'd-institution-refuses :lens "canon"
  :claim (canon 'launch-flows "A spec with several surfaces must say which surface carries each flow on each chain. This decision says same-chain and cross-chain Swap must be carried by another surface, but it names no surface, and native TRON appears nowhere in the file. It does not say whether paying, credit and savings run on both chains. launch-flows-need-owning-tests also asks for a browserless scenario and its own browser test per flow, and none is named for any of the nine flows here. The cost is that the claim another surface carries swaps cannot be checked against any file, so the launch could lose a flow without anyone having said so. Only the maintainer can accept the institution surface leaving out two of four required flows. Nothing in the file shows that decision."))

(objection 'o-institution-canon-4 :by "sonnet-canon" :to 'institution-needs-record :lens "canon"
  :claim (canon 'frontend-is-ui-only "Frontend code shows and asks; the runtime owns logic. This need asks the shared base to keep its own complete record of requests, votes and actions, for as long as the organisation chooses, in a form checkable against the signed history. The design's own because-clause says the runtime history is bounded and drops finished requests. A second store the wallet keeps beside the runtime's history is a parallel path (one-path-no-parallel). Nothing in the ground says such a store exists, so institution-record shows nothing at all (shows is empty) and institution-audit-flow ends with a record no runtime provides, which no-stubs-in-flows forbids offering. The cost is an auditor handed a record the organisation cannot prove complete. The maintainer decides where the record lives; d-institution-record asks that and has no answer, yet the screen, flow and need are written as if it were settled."))

(objection 'o-institution-canon-5 :by "sonnet-canon" :to 'd-institution-setup :lens "canon"
  :claim (canon 'one-path-no-parallel "The frontend carries no parallel implementation or fallback of runtime behaviour. The leaning is a setup sheet voted before the first account, with the safe choice of each setting applying until then. By its own because-clause, opening an account installs the automatic collateral policy, public listing and the response time in the same request, so the safe choice before the vote would have to be a second configuration path beside openAccount, or an interval in which the unsafe values are live. The institution defaults for auto top-up, unlisted accounts and response time are written as if this already worked. The cost is an organisation whose accounts pay fees under a rule nobody voted for in the first minutes, the thing the surface promises against. The decision is the maintainer's and its own changes-if names this problem; nothing in the file shows it answered."))

(objection 'o-institution-canon-6 :by "sonnet-canon" :to 'institution-default-delivery :lens "canon"
  :claim (canon 'htlc-constants-are-simnet "No real-funds routed payment on an EVM mainnet until per-jurisdiction expiry values are decided. This default picks the short expiry for every payment through a hub, so the surface chooses the very value the queue says nobody has decided, and treats it as risk-on nobody. institution-pay-flow signs pay-routed with no mention that on EVM mainnet it cannot be offered with real money yet. The cost is a board approving a run whose payments the queue says should not carry real funds. Direct payments and TRON are not covered by the rule. Which expiry applies per jurisdiction is the maintainer's; todo.md holds it as open and the file contains no decision about it."))
